This rule will trigger an unlimited amount of time rearming every refreshes, each time it triggers it will do so on Every selection|so you will always have the most uptdate information - this is the 'main' rule of the file and will store a range of data from TPD into stored values (shared), ||Because these values are (shared) Stored Values this means any of the data can then be used by other rules or refrerenced in other areas of Bet Angel ie, displayed on your one-click screen, ladder screen Guardian, the In-Play Trader screen  etc||The five regular stored values it stores along with the Stored Value name are as follows|Position in race = 'position'|Distance to Finish (meters - 'distance_to_finish'|Percentage of Race Distance Left to Run = 'percentage_remaining'|Distance to Leader = 'distance_to_leader' (see more about how the value is used near the bottom of this page)|Back Price of a Selection = 'back_price'|Speed (m/s) = speed  (This also has an adjustment to covert the speed into mph before the value is set)||The Speed (m/s) with the same adjustment to covert to mph is also stored into the History List 1|There are then two further Stored Values derived from range calculations ||The first of these stores a value named 'average_speed_5secs' by averaging the values in History List 1 from the last 5secs|The second of these stores a value named 'average_speed_10secs' by averaging the values in History List 1 from the last 10secs|||***The final three values are all for use on the In-Play trader screen, rather than try and explain here what they do once you've imported the IPT settings that accompany this file if you open up the editor and look for the stored values listed below you'll be able to see bettter what they are used for.||The first of these is a Stored Value named 'distance_to_leader_5'|this is created by multplying the 'distance_to_leader' stored value by 5||The second is a Stored Value named 'distance_to_leader_5a'|this is created by using the stored value 'distance_to_leader_5' minus a value of 3||The third is a Stored Value named 'distance_to_leader_5b'|this is created by using the stored value 'distance_to_leader_5' plus a value of 2|
