This rule is applied to the selection ranked 4 in the 'Custom Rank 1' list |(ie, the selection travelling second fastest based on the current speed update)||Each time it triggers it will store a value named (shared) named 'rank_speed'|This value is derived by taking the Stored Value named 'fastest_speed' minus the stored value named 'speed' for the market|||So the 'rank_speed' value is the difference between the runner traveling the fastest and the runner travelling forth fastest|||>>Every rule in this file triggers everytime the market is refreshed, so the next time it triggers it will start with the rule named 'Clear Fastest Time' again and Clear the 'Stored Value' named 'fastest_speed' for the market||The next few rules will then clear the stored values set on the runners ranked 2nd, 3rd and 4th in the 'Custom Ranking 1' list||This is so when the rule named 'Speed Data' trigger it can store a new set of speeds and then rank them, this all happens upto 5 times per second so you won't see any delays between the rules however it is important that they remain in their order otherwise the values you get will not be accurate
